      {
        "id": 87626,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-24T22:10:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You always leave a card out until it's fully resolved - if a card says \"play the top card of the deck\", you play said top card, and when that has fully resolved you put it wherever it's supposed to go (into the trash if it was a one-shot, into play if it's an ongoing, etc), and then go back to the first card. If \"play the top card\" was the last thing written on that card, it's then finished resolving so goes to the trash.</p>\n<p>You can get quite a pile if fighting someone like Ambuscade, who can chain many of these cards in a row. Akash'Bhuta is another one - I've had her play a Primeval Eruption, which puts out a bunch of limbs and then plays her top card, which is a Disrupt the Field, which destroys all environment cards and plays the top card of both the environment deck and her deck…which is another Primeval Eruption, which plays another card from her deck, meanwhile the environment card played from Disrupt the Field is a target which lets her play <span class=\"bbcode-i\">another</span> card, and so on. Finally you have this massiv epile of one-shots that she just played which all then go into the trash once you've played about a million cards. And then you put out End of Days or something and laugh :D.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:11:58.194Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 9318,
        "topic_slug": "shuffle-villian-deck-question",
        "display_username": "Ameena",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "You always leave a card out until it&#39;s fully resolved - if a card says &quot;play the top card of the deck&quot;, you play said top card, and when that has fully resolved you put it wherever it&#39;s supposed to go (into the trash if it was a one-shot, into play if it&#39;s an ongoing, etc), and then go back to the first card. If &quot;play the top card&quot; was the last thing written on that card, it&#39;s then finished resolving so goes to the trash.\n\nYou can get quite a pile if fighting someone like Ambuscade, who can chain many of these cards in a row. Akash&#39;Bhuta is another one - I&#39;ve had her play a Primeval Eruption, which puts out a bunch of limbs and then plays her top card, which is a Disrupt the Field, which destroys all environment cards and plays the top card of both the environment deck and her deck...which is another Primeval Eruption, which plays another card from her deck, meanwhile the environment card played from Disrupt the Field is a target which lets her play [i]another[/i] card, and so on. Finally you have this massiv epile of one-shots that she just played which all then go into the trash once you&#39;ve played about a million cards. And then you put out End of Days or something and laugh :D.\n",
