      {
        "id": 87627,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-25T09:06:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>For an example of how it works, today I played Akash'Bhuta, and she brought out Disrupt the Field.&nbsp; This destroyed all Environment cards, then played a Villain card, and would then play an Environment card...except that the villain card played was Primeval Eruption, which brought out two more of A'B's Limbs.&nbsp; When the Limbs came into play, two cards were dsicarded from the Environment deck.&nbsp; Then Primeval Eruption played another card, which was Earth's Sacrifice, destroying two hero ongoings and discarding two more Environment cards.&nbsp; Only then did Earth's Sacrifice go to the trash, and then Primeval Eruption, and then we completed Disrupt the Field's effect by playing an Environment card (from a significantly depleted deck, thanks to all that discarding), and finally Disrupt the Field went to the trash.&nbsp; It would have been very possible for either or both decks to reshuffle during this process; had there been no cards in A'B's deck after Primeval Eruption resolved, the bonus card that it plays would have come from a reshuffled trash, but neither Disrupt the Field nor Primeval Eruption would be in the reshuffle.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:11:58.286Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
